 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Try saying You' done good things, and we believe in you. Small acts of kindness count too. A birthday party they remember years later, a special outing you both enjoy, or small gifts that mean something like a brush for your mom. Then ask her to pick one person from each of you and your partner, and one friend each for a group outing. That way, everyone gets a little something. And maybe lead with the idea of a birthday party rather than scaled down gifts, so it doesn't feel like a betrayal. People respond well to being asked.",
